      "widgets_values": [
        "Realistic live-action cinematic look, contemplative arthouse drama, practical film photography style, quiet coastal harbor at dusk, anamorphic lens, shallow depth of field, subtle film grain, gentle sea mist, restrained cinematic color grading with cool blue twilight and warm amber sunset highlights, natural lighting, realistic textures, calm atmospheric mood, premium live-action aesthetic, slow deliberate pacing.\n\nScene overview: A young man stands alone at the edge of an almost deserted harbor as dusk gradually fades into early evening. He quietly smokes a cigarette while watching several ships slowly sail across the calm water toward the horizon. The scene is reflective and melancholic, emphasizing solitude, silence, and the passage of time. The nearly empty harbor feels peaceful, with only distant ship horns and gentle waves breaking the stillness.\n\nStoryboard (each shot a separate scene, smooth cinematic cuts):\n\n[0s–2s] Shot 1: Wide establishing shot from behind the young man leaning lightly against the harbor railing. The sky glows with the final colors of sunset while distant cargo ships slowly cross the calm water. Thin cigarette smoke drifts upward in the cool evening breeze.\n[2s–4s] Shot 2: Medium side profile. He slowly raises the cigarette to his lips, takes a long drag, then lowers his hand without looking away from the horizon. The smoke curls through the fading golden-blue light while the ships continue gliding silently in the background.\n[4s–6s] Shot 3: Close-up of his face. His expression remains calm and thoughtful, illuminated by soft twilight. The ember at the tip of the cigarette briefly glows brighter as he exhales a slow cloud of smoke that dissolves into the sea mist.\n[6s–8s] Shot 4: Over-the-shoulder shot looking across the harbor. Several ships move steadily toward the horizon, their navigation lights beginning to appear as the sky darkens. Gentle ripples shimmer with reflections from scattered harbor lights.\n[8s–10s] Shot 5: Wide cinematic closing shot. The camera slowly pulls backward, revealing the vast empty harbor with the young man standing alone in silhouette. The ships continue disappearing into the twilight as the final traces of daylight fade from the sky.\n\nCamera: Slow cinematic dolly movements, gentle push-ins and pull-backs, stable handheld realism with subtle natural motion, clean cuts between shots, no rapid movements, soft parallax, realistic depth of field, patient cinematic pacing.\n\nAudio: Gentle ocean waves, distant ship engines, occasional low foghorn, soft coastal wind, faint seagulls far in the distance, subtle ambient cinematic score built around soft piano and warm strings, with natural harbor ambience remaining dominant throughout.\n\nNo text, subtitles, logos, watermarks, animation, cartoon rendering, exaggerated visual effects, or overly-CG appearance. Preserve realistic live-action textures, authentic human movement, natural cigarette smoke physics, cinematic lighting, and a quiet, introspective atmosphere.",
